Package: ReMPCA
Title: Regularized Principal Component Analysis for Hybrid Data
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: c(
    person("Mobina", "Pourmoshir", , "mobina.pourmoshir@marquette.edu", role = c("aut", "cre", "cph")),
    person("Mehdi", "Maadooliat", , "mehdi.maadooliat@mu.edu", role = "aut")
    )
Description: Regularized principal component analysis for hybrid data, in which
    functional variables (curves, images, or other gridded objects) and
    non-functional (scalar or vector) variables are observed on a common set of
    rows. Components are estimated by a regularized rank-one power algorithm
    that allows block-specific smoothness and sparsity penalties on the
    loadings and, for two-way data with ordered rows, on the scores. Smoothing
    parameters are selected by generalized cross-validation and sparsity levels
    by K-fold cross-validation. Ordinary, sparse, smooth functional,
    multivariate functional, hybrid, and two-way regularized principal
    component analysis arise as special cases. The approach builds on Huang,
    Shen and Buja (2008) <doi:10.1214/08-EJS218>, Shen and Huang (2008)
    <doi:10.1016/j.jmva.2007.06.007>, and Huang, Shen and Buja (2009)
    <doi:10.1198/jasa.2009.tm08024>.
